For **this app**, don't think of it as a todo app.

Think of it as:

> **A personal life maintenance dashboard.**
>
> Calm. Minimal. Information-dense.
> Almost like a mix between Google Calendar + Apple Health + Linear.

---

# First UI Principle

Your users should never ask:

* Where do I click?
* What does this number mean?

Instead, they should immediately see:

```text
Curtains
72 days ago
Next due in 8 days
```

No calculations. No clutter.

---

# The Design Style I would copy

## 1. Apple Health

Very simple cards.

```
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ 🪟 Curtains                 │
│                             │
│ 72 days                     │
│ since last wash             │
│                             │
│ Due in 8 days               │
│                             │
│           [Mark Done]       │
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

Characteristics:

* lots of whitespace
* rounded corners (16-20px)
* subtle shadows
* muted colors
* typography does most of the work

---

## 2. Linear.app

[Linear](https://linear.app?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

This is probably the closest inspiration.

Take from it:

* monochrome palette
* smooth animations
* tiny hover effects
* minimal borders
* dark mode first

Avoid bright colors.

---

## 3. Apple Reminders

Instead of giant tables.

Use grouped sections:

```
Today
------------------
□ AC Filter
□ Water Plants

Upcoming
------------------
□ Curtains (8 days)

Completed Recently
------------------
✓ Health Checkup
    24 days ago
```

