# If I were giving Claude Code one UI instruction, it would be:

```text
Build the UI like a calm, premium personal dashboard.

Use shadcn/ui as the component foundation.
Use Tailwind CSS and TypeScript.
Prefer cards over tables.
Use generous whitespace.
Dark mode by default.
Avoid bright colors and excessive animations.
Take visual inspiration from Apple Health and Linear.
The app should feel like an external memory for life maintenance, not a task manager.
```

For a solo developer using **Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind**, this is currently one of the safest and most professional stacks:

**shadcn/ui + Tailwind + Framer Motion (light use) + Lucide icons + Inter/Geist font**. It looks modern out of the box and requires almost no formal UI/UX background to produce a polished result. ([Shadcn UI][1])

